{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>See.</b> Attend, and do not hide Your face from him in this matter." "<b>You say to me, 'Lead this people.'</b> When You said to me: 'Go, ascend from here — you and the people.'" "<b>And You have not made known to me whom You will send with me.</b> For when You said 'I will send a messenger before you and I will drive out,' this is to be understood for when we enter the land — but on the way we have with us neither Your Shekhinah nor any messenger." "<b>And You said, 'I have known you by name.'</b> And from this it follows that when You imposed upon me to lead them on the way, this was not by way of abandonment — as in 'And I said, I will not tend you; the dying shall die and the perishing shall perish' (Zechariah 11:9) — but rather You desired that I myself be the messenger who goes before the camp of Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:55.044837589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}